With shared hosting, one IP address is shared among many different web servers with different domain names. With reverse 
IP lookup, starting from a domain name or an IP address, you can find the other domain names using a specific IP address(es).

In the figure below, we used reverse IP lookup to find other servers sharing the same IP addresses used. Therefore, it is 
important to note that knowing the IP address does not necessarily lead to a single website.

Threat Intelligence Platform requires you to provide a domain name or an IP address, and it will launch a series of tests 
from malware checks to WHOIS and DNS queries. The WHOIS and DNS results are similar to the results we would get using whois 
and dig, but Threat Intelligence Platform presents them in a more readable and visually appealing way.

